      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osborne%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Osborne lies on the north side of the South Fork Solomon River in the Smoky Hills region of the Great Plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osborne%2C_Kansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Osborne County Historical Museum maintains a one-room school house built in 1912 on its site.",
